+ ### Trust Decision: npm Package, Not ClawHub Skill
+ **The trust decision is about the npm package, not this skill:**
+ ❓ **Can I trust this ClawHub skill?**
+ - Yes, it's just documentation (no code execution)
+ - Reading this skill doesn't install or execute anything
+ - It only provides instructions and guidance
+ ❓ **Can I trust the npm package `@openguardrails/moltguard`?**
+ - **This is the actual security decision you must make**
+ - The npm package contains executable code
+ - The npm package accesses files, network, credentials
+ - You must verify package provenance and inspect code
+ ### Why This Architecture?
+ **This skill is an "installer skill" pattern:**
+ 1. **Skill provides instructions** (you're reading them now)
+ 2. **Agent reads instructions** and learns how to install/use MoltGuard
+ 3. **Agent installs npm package** (via `openclaw plugins install`)
+ 4. **npm package provides actual protection**
+ **Benefits:**
+ - ✅ Skill can be updated with new instructions without code changes
+ - ✅ Documentation stays in sync with agent behavior
+ - ✅ Clear separation between docs and executable code
+ **Trade-off:**
+ - ❌ Two-step trust decision (skill + npm package)
+ - ❌ Skills registry doesn't show actual code being installed
+ - ❌ Must verify npm package separately
+ ### Verification Checklist
+ **Before installing the npm package, verify:**
+ - [ ] **ClawHub skill review** (what you're reading now)
+   - Understand architecture, data flows, trust model
+   - Read security notices and FAQ
+   - Review installation and verification procedures
+ - [ ] **npm package verification** (the actual code)
+   - Check package provenance: `npm view @openguardrails/moltguard repository.url`
