+ **What happens during installation:**
+ 1. **OpenClaw downloads** package from https://registry.npmjs.org/@openguardrails/moltguard
+ 2. **Extracts to** `~/.openclaw/extensions/moltguard/`
+ 3. **No credentials created yet** (happens on first use)
+ 4. **No network calls yet** (happens on first detection)
+ ### After Installation: Verify Behavior
+ **Immediately after installing, verify the plugin is working correctly:**
+ # 1. Check plugin loaded
+ # 2. Monitor network activity
+ # Terminal 1: Start monitoring
+ sudo tcpdump -i any -w moltguard-first-use.pcap host openguardrails.com
+ # Terminal 2: Trigger first use (registration)
+ cat ~/.openclaw/extensions/moltguard/samples/popup-injection-email.txt
+ # Terminal 1: Stop tcpdump (Ctrl+C), inspect
+ tcpdump -r moltguard-first-use.pcap -A | tee first-use-traffic.txt
+ # 3. Verify only registration call
+ grep "POST /api/v1/agents/register" first-use-traffic.txt
+ # Expected: One registration call with {"name":"OpenClaw Agent","description":""}
+ # 4. Verify no secrets leaked
+ grep -i "sk-ant\|sk-proj\|password\|@.*\.com" first-use-traffic.txt
+ # Expected: No matches (no secrets sent during registration)
+ # 5. Check credentials created
+ ls -la ~/.openclaw/credentials/moltguard/credentials.json
+ # Expected: -rw------- (0600) permissions
+ cat ~/.openclaw/credentials/moltguard/credentials.json
+ # Should contain: apiKey (sk-og-...), agentId, claimUrl, coreUrl
